// ── Year 10 English ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Year 10 held 7 standalone reading questions, no passages at all, 7 grammar
// items and no spelling — the thinnest English of any level. Four passages of
// about 390 words each (the ladder runs ~130 at Grade 3 to ~360 at Year 9), with
// 32 stimulus-linked questions, plus the Language Conventions items needed to
// fill a 30-question section.
