    format: 'extended_response',
    calculator_allowed: true,
    practice_set: 3,
    question_text: "A tank initially contains 50 L of pure water. Brine containing 0.5 kg of salt per litre flows in at 4 L min⁻¹, and the well-mixed solution flows out at 2 L min⁻¹. The tank holds 100 L. Let \\(Q\\) kg be the amount of salt in the tank \\(t\\) minutes after the brine starts to flow.",
    parts: [
      { label: "a", prompt: "Show that \\(\\dfrac{dQ}{dt} = 2 - \\dfrac{Q}{25 + t}\\) while the tank is filling.", marks: 2, expected_answer: "In: \\(0.5 \\times 4 = 2\\) kg min⁻¹. Volume \\(50 + 2t\\), so out: \\(\\frac{2Q}{50 + 2t} = \\frac{Q}{25 + t}\\).", explanation: "1 mark for the inflow rate, 1 mark for the outflow using the changing volume.", lines: 6 },
      { label: "b", prompt: "Verify that \\(Q = \\dfrac{t(t + 50)}{t + 25}\\) satisfies the differential equation and the initial condition.", marks: 2, expected_answer: "\\(Q(0) = 0\\), and \\(\\frac{dQ}{dt} = \\frac{t^2 + 50t + 1250}{(t + 25)^2} = 2 - \\frac{t(t + 50)}{(t + 25)^2}\\).", explanation: "\\(2 - \\frac{Q}{25 + t} = \\frac{2(t + 25)^2 - t(t + 50)}{(t + 25)^2} = \\frac{t^2 + 50t + 1250}{(t + 25)^2}\\), which equals \\(\\frac{dQ}{dt}\\) found by the quotient rule. 1 mark for each check.", lines: 6 },
      { label: "c", prompt: "Find the time at which the tank is full and the amount of salt in it at that time.", marks: 2, expected_answer: "\\(t = 25\\) min; 37.5 kg", explanation: "\\(50 + 2t = 100\\) gives \\(t = 25\\); \\(Q(25) = \\frac{25 \\times 75}{50} = 37.5\\). 1 mark each.", lines: 6 },
      { label: "d", prompt: "Find the time at which the concentration of salt in the tank first reaches 0.3 kg L⁻¹, in minutes correct to two decimal places.", marks: 2, expected_answer: "14.53 min", explanation: "Solve \\(\\dfrac{t(t + 50)}{(t + 25)(50 + 2t)} = 0.3\\): \\(t^2 + 50t - 937.5 = 0\\), so \\(t \\approx 14.53\\). 1 mark for the equation, 1 mark for the value.", lines: 6 },
      { label: "e", prompt: "When the tank is full, the brine is replaced by pure water flowing in at 2 L min⁻¹, so the volume stays at 100 L. Find the time, measured from when the brine started, at which the tank contains 10 kg of salt. Give your answer in minutes correct to one decimal place.", marks: 2, expected_answer: "91.1 min", explanation: "Now \\(\\frac{dQ}{dt} = -\\frac{2Q}{100}\\) with \\(Q = 37.5\\) at \\(t = 25\\), so \\(Q = 37.5e^{-0.02(t - 25)}\\). \\(Q = 10\\) gives \\(t = 25 + 50\\loge(3.75) \\approx 91.1\\). 1 mark for the model, 1 mark for the time.", lines: 6 },
    ],
    explanation: "See the worked solutions for each part.",
    curriculum_code: 'VCE-SM-U34-AOS4',
