    question_text: "The energy levels of hydrogen are \\(E_n = -\\frac{13.6}{n^2}\\) eV. The wavelength of the photon emitted when an electron in hydrogen moves from the \\(n = 4\\) level to the \\(n = 2\\) level is closest to",
