    topic: 'life_science',
    year_level: 'grade_6',
    difficulty: 'advanced',
    question_text: "On hydroponic farms, lettuces are grown with their roots in flowing water that has nutrients dissolved in it. No soil is used at all.\nWhat does this show about what plants need from soil?",
    options: ["Plants do not need any nutrients at all to grow.","Plants need the water and nutrients that soil holds, not the soil itself.","Lettuces take in all of their water through their leaves instead of their roots.","Plants only need soil while they are still seeds."],
    correct_index: 1,
    explanation: "The lettuces grow well with no soil, so soil itself is not essential. What plants take from soil is water and dissolved nutrients, and a hydroponic farm supplies both directly to the roots.",
