    topic: 'life_science',
    year_level: 'grade_6',
    difficulty: 'proficient',
    question_text: "A farmer in Tasmania grows tomatoes in a glasshouse during spring. Outside, the nights are often colder than 8 °C.\nWhy does the glasshouse help the tomatoes grow?",
    options: ["It stops any light from reaching the plants, so they can rest at night.","It keeps all of the air away from the plants.","It keeps the plants warmer, closer to the temperature tomatoes need.","It makes each day several hours longer for the plants."],
    correct_index: 2,
    explanation: "Tomatoes grow poorly in cold conditions. A glasshouse lets sunlight in and traps warmth, so the plants stay warmer, especially at night, than they would outside.",
