    topic: 'earth_space',
    year_level: 'grade_6',
    difficulty: 'proficient',
    question_text: "Soon after people at a beach feel the ground shake, the sea suddenly drains away from the shore, much further than at a normal low tide.\nWhat should they do?",
    options: ["Walk out to look at the sea floor and shells while they are uncovered.","Move quickly to high ground or well inland, as a tsunami may be coming.","Stay on the beach, because the water has moved away from the shore.","Sit on the sand and wait until the water comes back."],
    correct_index: 1,
    explanation: "The sea suddenly pulling back after an earthquake is a natural warning sign of a tsunami. The water can return as a powerful surge within minutes, so people should head for high ground straight away.",
