    topic: 'earth_space',
    year_level: 'year_10',
    difficulty: 'advanced',
    question_text: "Students model the greenhouse effect with two sealed plastic bottles under a lamp, one containing air and one containing extra carbon dioxide. The bottle with extra carbon dioxide warms a little more.\nWhich is the most important limitation of this model?",
    options: ["The lamp gives off visible light, while the Sun gives off only infrared radiation.","Carbon dioxide can only absorb heat when it has been cooled into a liquid.","The model leaves out water vapour, which is not a greenhouse gas.","A sealed bottle also warms by trapping warm air, and its CO₂ level is far higher than in the real atmosphere."],
    correct_index: 3,
    explanation: "Much of the warming in both bottles comes from stopping warm air from rising away, which is not how the atmosphere traps heat, and the CO₂ concentration is many times the real one. The Sun gives off mostly visible light, and water vapour is in fact an important greenhouse gas.",
