    topic: 'earth_space',
    year_level: 'year_10',
    difficulty: 'proficient',
    question_text: "Over 20 years, each tonne of methane traps about 80 times as much heat as a tonne of carbon dioxide. A dairy farm adds a seaweed supplement to its cows' feed, which cuts the farm's methane emissions by 2 tonnes a year.\nAbout how many tonnes of carbon dioxide would the farm need to cut each year to have the same effect over 20 years?",
    options: ["40 tonnes","78 tonnes","82 tonnes","160 tonnes"],
    correct_index: 3,
    explanation: "Each tonne of methane is equivalent to about 80 tonnes of carbon dioxide, so for 2 tonnes of methane: 2 × 80 = 160 tonnes. Adding 80 and 2, or dividing 80 by 2, are the common slips.",
